description:
Whether C_d(K) extends to a coherent presentation, and at what cost.

Expected shape, to be confirmed or refuted:
- the presentation itself is canonical at every d: rank-2 intervals are hexagons and squares, each with exactly two directed paths, so the relations are forced with no choice;
- coherence needs codim-3 data, whose interval is 3-dimensional and whose boundary is a 2-sphere with no canonical bisection, so a minimal homotopy basis requires a choice;
- a canonical but redundant coherent presentation does exist: take every parallel pair of 2-paths over each codim-3 interval.

Wanted: settle which of these hold. The distinction that matters is existence versus minimality.
